    "result_text": "All 270 tests pass, including the new Cp08 test. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created without a registration date, it now defaults to today's date and is returned in the owner response as `registrationDate` in ISO format (`YYYY-MM-DD`).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`Owner` model** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (column `registration_date`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schema** \u2014 added `registration_date DATE` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (`hsqldb` \u2014 used by tests, plus `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`).\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and serializes as ISO. MapStruct maps it `Owner \u2194 OwnerDto` automatically by name.\n\n4. **`BuildOwner`** function \u2014 the `POST /api/owners` pipeline's first step now sets `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the built owner has none, before the owner is saved.\n\nThe registration date flows through the existing `build \u2192 ensureUnique \u2192 save \u2192 respond` OfficeFloor pipeline, is persisted, and is read back on `GET /api/owners/{id}`. The one MapStruct warning about an unmapped target on the `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` mapping is expected (the field is response-only) and harmless.",
